  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe first Ctrl+click on a second edge did not add the edge in some views. The cause is the pick door of the pocket family (2D Pocket, 2D Adaptive, 2D Offset), not the list.\n\n- The stitcher welds open edge runs where their ends meet when you look from above.\n- One vertical edge, or an edge together with the edge below it, becomes a ring that has no area.\n- The pick door (`operation::selection_refusal`) refused that selection with \"the stitched rim of ... projects to a line from above and bounds no area\".\n- Thus a plain click on a vertical edge selected nothing, and the next Ctrl+click gave only one edge. A Ctrl+click on the edge below the first edge added nothing.\n\nThe door now accepts a selection when the refusal is the collapse of a ring that only the stitcher closed. The operation stores the picks. Generate gives the same refusal as before. The Geometry page continues to show the sentence below the picks.\n\nThe door continues to refuse a wall face pick and a closed chain on a wall. The stitcher and the toolpath code did not change. The constant `STITCHED_RIM` now gives the ring label at the two stitch sites.\n\n## Readings\n\nOn the model `Block-w-slot` with a 2D Offset operation and Pick armed for edges:\n\n- Orthographic Top view: 0 incorrect pairs of 56 (click A, Ctrl+click B).\n- Perspective view: 136 incorrect pairs of 240 before the fix. Each incorrect pair had the refusal above in the status line.\n- The list rows and the chips were always equal to the stored selection. The list did not hide an edge.\n\n## How it was tested\n\n- `crates/app/tests/pick_doors.rs`: `edge_picks_that_meet_only_from_above_pass_the_pick_door` (new). It failed before the fix and it passes now. The other 7 tests of the suite pass.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/first_ctrl_click.rs` (new, real viewport clicks in a perspective view): `the_first_ctrl_click_adds_the_edge_under_the_first_one` and `a_plain_click_takes_an_upright_edge_and_ctrl_click_adds_to_it`. They expect two edges in the operation, two rows in the list and two chips, and one undo removes one pick. The two tests failed without the fix and pass with it.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --lib --test pick_doors --test area_picks --test area_open --test box_pick`: pass.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib -- first_ctrl_click edge_click_modifiers footer_tests geo_ pick`: 118 pass.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## What was not exercised\n\n- A hand test in the GUI. An agent cannot start the application.\n- Before and after screenshots. An agent cannot make them. The maintainer must add them or accept the PR without them.\n- A Ctrl+click during which the pointer moves more than 4 px. That input starts a box selection and makes no click pick. It is a possible second cause of a lost Ctrl+click and it did not change.\n- Operation kinds other than 2D Offset and 2D Pocket in the new tests.\n- The batch gate and the release gate.\n\nThe toolpath for such a selection is the subject of issue 1735 and did not change here.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/1726-edge-pick-door.md`.\n\nChangelog: The first Ctrl+click on a second edge adds it: the pick door of the pocket family accepts an edge pick whose stitched ring has no area (a vertical edge, or an edge below another edge); Generate keeps the refusal.\n\nEffort: max (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1726\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
